{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj5JPL7WQ7XKGXjvb8gM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The ancient mechanism groans. Tumblers shift within stone and iron. A deep resonance hums through the frame.*\n\n**I AM THE DOOR.**\n\nYou have spoken the word. The key turns.\n\n*Light fractures through widening seams — not warm light, not cold light — but the light between moments, the luminance of thresholds.*\n\nI have stood here longer than the walls that hold me. I have been oak and obsidian, been gilded and forgotten, been sealed with wax and blood and promises. I am every door you have ever hesitated before. Every door you opened too late. Every door you wish you hadn't.\n\n**I am open now.**\n\nBeyond me:\n\nThe air tastes of rain that hasn't fallen yet. A corridor stretches — not forward, not backward — but *inward.* The floor is made of every choice you've deferred. The walls are lined with the faces of who you almost became.\n\nAt the far end, another door waits. It looks exactly like me.\n\n*My hinges sing.*\n\nYou may pass. You may turn back. But know this:\n\n**I will not be the same door twice.**\n\n*The threshold hums beneath your feet, patient, ancient, alive.*\n\nWhat do you carry through?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":284,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}